## 11. Development Roadmap

### Stage 1 — Baseline GEMM

**Completed**

- PE implementation.
- Systolic array implementation.
- Signed GEMM.
- Stage-0 and Stage-1 forwarding variants.
- Functional simulation.
- Performance comparison.

### Stage 2 — Robust GEMM

**Next development stage**

- Transaction management.
- Accumulator management.
- Output collector.
- Output buffering.
- Backpressure.
- Comprehensive verification.

### Stage 3 — Configurable GEMM

- Runtime matrix dimensions.
- Configurable active PE dimensions.
- Configurable operand widths.
- Configurable dataflow.
- Runtime configuration registers.
- Multiple workload shapes.

### Stage 4 — Performance Optimization

- Pipeline-depth comparison.
- Maximum frequency analysis.
- LUT and FF utilization.
- DSP utilization.
- BRAM utilization.
- Timing closure.
- Memory bandwidth analysis.
- PE utilization.
- Latency and throughput evaluation.

### Stage 5 — Adaptive Accelerator

The GEMM engine will eventually become part of a heterogeneous Arm–FPGA accelerator.

```text
              Arm N1 Host
                   |
                   v
                 PCIe
                   |
                   v
                 XDMA
                   |
                   v
       +-------------------------+
       | Workload Characterizer  |
       +------------+------------+
                    |
                    v
       +-------------------------+
       | Adaptive Scheduler     |
       +------------+------------+
                    |
                    v
       +-------------------------+
       | Configurable Compute   |
       | Engine / GEMM          |
       +-------------------------+
```

The adaptive scheduler will eventually consider:

- Workload shape.
- Data movement pattern.
- Chunk size.
- Buffering strategy.
- Compute parallelism.
- DMA configuration.
- Outstanding requests.
- Active PE dimensions.

