## 13. Conclusion

This project explores two microarchitectural implementations of an output-stationary systolic GEMM accelerator.

The Stage-0 forwarding implementation provides lower cycle-level latency and higher simulated throughput in the current configuration. The Stage-1 forwarding implementation adds an extra registered forwarding stage, potentially offering better timing isolation.

The final architectural decision will be based on synthesized performance, including frequency, resource utilization, timing, and power—not simulation cycle count alone.

The current GEMM accelerator establishes the computational foundation for the broader objective:

**Adaptive Data-Movement and Accelerator Architecture for Heterogeneous Arm–FPGA Systems.**
